<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Ailech</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 1185 CE (approx.) · capital Grianan of Aileach</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Kingdom of the northern Uí Néill based at the stone fort of Grianan of Aileach, whose Cenél nEógain kings often held the high kingship of Ireland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ailech emerged in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a> as the kingdom of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a>, descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niall-of-the-nine-hostages">Niall of the Nine Hostages</a> who expanded into the north-west in the 5th and 6th centuries. It took its name from the hilltop stone fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grianan-of-aileach">Grianan of Aileach</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inishowen">Inishowen</a> peninsula, which served as a royal centre.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom was dominated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-neogain">Cenél nEógain</a>, who displaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-conaill">Cenél Conaill</a> from the kingship in the 8th century and alternated the high kingship with the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a>. Kings such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aed-findliath">Áed Findliath</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niall-glundub">Niall Glúndub</a>, killed fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> in 919, were among the most powerful in Ireland. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mac-lochlainn-dynasty">Mac Lochlainn</a> line, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muirchertach-mac-lochlainn">Muirchertach Mac Lochlainn</a>, held the high kingship in the 12th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1101 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muirchertach-ua-briain">Muirchertach Ua Briain</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Munster</a> demolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grianan-of-aileach">Grianan of Aileach</a> in revenge for an earlier attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kincora">Kincora</a>. Power within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-neogain">Cenél nEógain</a> passed from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mac-lochlainn-dynasty">Mac Lochlainns</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/o-neill-dynasty">Ua Néill</a>, and the kingdom of Ailech became the O'Neill kingdom of Tír Eógain, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-tir-eoghain">Tyrone</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-ailech.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Ailech" width="320" height="408"><figcaption>Image: Erakis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ireland900.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>450 CE – 1185 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Grianan of Aileach</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Áed Findliath, Niall Glúndub, Muirchertach Mac Lochlainn</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Irish, later Middle Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a>, <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ailech, Aileach, Northern Ui Neill</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=818&amp;focus=kingdom-of-ailech" aria-label="Kingdom of Ailech on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4517 297 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Ailech lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4837 553L4851 567M4837 553L4821 563"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4851 567h0M4821 563h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4837 553h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4837 553h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Grianan of Aileach. <a href="/atlas?year=818&amp;focus=kingdom-of-ailech">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
